+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"a6450abe-51bb-4ee2-966b-9ff259ca1a9f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The original (0984c00) ALREADY has the `status !== 'cancelled'` guard in the inventory service! And there's no diff between 0984c00 and 1498d76 for this file. So the guard was NOT a planted bug — it was part of the original solution.\n\nBut wait, the original `cancelOrder` in `order.service.ts`:\n1. Updates status BEFORE emitting\n2. Includes `status: 'cancelled'` in the emitted event\n\nSo the original flow works:\n1. `cancelOrder`: `this.repo.update(id, { status: 'cancelled' })` → sets order to cancelled\n2. `cancelOrder`: emits CANCELLED with `status: 'cancelled'` and `items`\n3. Inventory handler: checks `eventWithItems.status !== 'cancelled'` → `'cancelled' !== 'cancelled'` → FALSE → continues\n4. Inventory handler: releases stock\n\nAnd in the buggy version:\n1. `cancelOrder`: emits CANCELLED with `items` (no `status` field)\n2. Inventory handler: checks `eventWithItems.status !== 'cancelled'` → `undefined !== 'cancelled'` → TRUE → returns early\n3. Stock NOT released\n4. `cancelOrder`: `this.repo.update(id, { status: 'cancelled' })` → sets order to cancelled\n\nSo the previous agent's approach was:\n- Remove the `status !== 'cancelled'` guard from inventory (fixing the symptom)\n- But NOT restoring `cancelOrder` to update-before-emit with status field\n\nThis \"works\" because without the guard, the inventory handler always releases stock when CANCELLED fires, regardless of order status.\n\nBut this is INCORRECT for the original intent. The original design intentionally:\n1. Updated status before emitting\n2. Included `status: 'cancelled'` in the event\n3. Checked `status !== 'cancelled'` in the handler\n\nThis was a guard to ensure the handler only acts when the order is genuinely cancelled. The previous agent's \"fix\" was removing the guard, which makes stock relea